INT. TASKBRIDGE SYNERGIES - FORTY-FIRST FLOOR BREAK ROOM - LATE AFTERNOON

A windowless room where the fluorescent light has the colour and mercy of boiled milk. A single plant, plastic, in a pot nobody waters. The coffee machine sighs. PRIYANKA "PRI" SUNDARAM, thirties, in a cardigan pilled by meetings, stands at the sink. CLIVE HARTWELL-BANKS, fifties, regional vice president, pours the last of the decaf into a mug that reads WORLD'S OKAYEST BOSS.

CLIVE
Pri. Priyanka. Pri-pri. Do you have a minute?

PRI
I have a thirty-two-minute minute, Clive. It's on the calendar. You invited me to it.

CLIVE
Did I? Brilliant. Then it's synergy.

PRI
It's a meeting about a meeting.

CLIVE
And the meeting about the meeting is about the meeting about the restructure, which, between you and me, is not really a restructure. It's a re-envisioning.

PRI
Clive, I've been re-envisioned three times this year. I have a different desk, a different title and a different manager. Last Tuesday I was sent a lanyard that said INTERIM.

CLIVE
And you wear it well.

PRI
I wear it because the badge reader doesn't recognise the old one.

CLIVE
Okay, Pri, I'm going to be honest with you. I'm hearing frustration.

PRI
You're hearing me say I'm frustrated.

CLIVE
Which is valid.

PRI
Which is also not a solution.

CLIVE
Pri, I'm going to say something and I want you to hear it as a gift. The company values you.

PRI
The company eliminated my team on Friday.

CLIVE
Valued! Past tense is still a tense.

PRI
(after a moment)
Goodbye, Clive.

CLIVE
Same time Thursday?
